>
  <h2>What this is</h2>
  <p>
    Acute musculoskeletal injuries — sprains, strains, disc episodes, post-surgical recovery —
    are interruptions, not endings. The decisions made in the first 48–72 hours after an injury
    have an outsized effect on recovery trajectory, yet most men either push through inappropriately
    or shut down entirely.
  </p>
  <p>
    The Muscle pillar includes a structured acute-injury response protocol that covers
    triage, load management, and return-to-activity planning. Dr. Mundheim's 30 years of
    clinical chiropractic and sports performance background underpins this framework.
  </p>

  <h2>Our approach</h2>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Triage Framework</h3>
      <p>Differentiate what can be managed conservatively from what needs imaging or specialist referral — fast.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Active Recovery Protocol</h3>
      <p>Movement within pain-free range is almost always superior to rest. Graded exposure starts Day 1.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Load Management Plan</h3>
      <p>Modify, don't delete, your training. Keep metabolic and neural adaptations alive during recovery.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card">
      <h3>Return-to-Performance</h3>
      <p>Structured milestones before returning to full intensity — reducing re-injury risk significantly.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</SolutionPage>
